{title: 153 - Prince of Peace, Control My Will}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #153 • TRYGGARE KAN INGEN VARA • 14.14}
{lyricist: Anon}
{composer: Swedish folk melody}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 153}
{meta: tune TRYGGARE KAN INGEN VARA}
{meta: meter 14.14}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D/F#]Prince [G]of [D/A]Peace, control my [Em/G]will, Bid [G]this [A7/C#]struggling [D/A]heart [G]be still;
[Bm]Bid my fears [C#7]and [F#m/C#]doubtings cease, [F/C]Hush my [Em/B]spirit [A7/G]into [D/F#]peace.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D/F#]Thou hast [Bm]bought [Em/G]me [G]with [D#/A#]Thy [G]blood,
[D/F#]Opened [Bm]wide [Em/G]the [G]gate [D#/A#]to [G]God;
[Bm]Peace, I [F#m/C#]ask, but [F/C]peace [A7/G]must be,
[Bm]Lord, [C#7]in [F#m/A]being [F/C]one [A7/G]with Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D/F#]May Thy [Bm]will, [Em/G]not [G]mine, [D#/A#]be [G]done,
[D/F#]May Thy [Bm]will [Em/G]and [G]mine [D#/A#]be [G]one;
[Bm]Chase these [F#m/C#]doubtings [F/C]from [A7/G]my heart,
[Bm]Now Thy [F#m/C#]perfect [F/C]peace [A7/G]impart.
{end_of_verse}
